Leetcode:- 179

Given a list of non-negative integers nums, arrange them such that they form the largest number and return it.
Since the result may be very large, so you need to return a string instead of an integer.

Example 1:

Input: nums = [10,2]
Output: "210"


problem:-

❌ Issue 1: Comparator inside class
bool cmp(string a ,string b)

👉 This won’t work with sort as written, because:

Member functions need an object (this)
sort expects a static or external function

approach:-

1) using static

class Solution {
public:
    static bool cmp(string a ,string b){
        return a+b>b+a;
    }
    string largestNumber(vector<int>& nums) {
        vector<string>ans;
        for(auto it:nums){
            ans.push_back(to_string(it));
        }

        sort(ans.begin(),ans.end(),cmp);

        if(ans[0]=="0") return "0";

        string result="";
        for(auto it: ans){
            result+=it;
        }
      return result;
    }
};

2) using lambda function (prefer this)-

class Solution {
public:
    
    string largestNumber(vector<int>& nums) {
        vector<string>ans;
        for(auto it:nums){
            ans.push_back(to_string(it));
        }

        sort(ans.begin(),ans.end(),[](const auto &a,const auto &b){
            return a+b>b+a;
        });

        if(ans[0]=="0") return "0";

        string result="";
        for(auto it: ans){
            result+=it;
        }
      return result;
    }
};
